WEBVTT

00:01.480 --> 00:04.900
<b>July 3rd, Unified Year 1927 Imperial Capital</b>

00:25.050 --> 00:26.380
<b>Lt. Colonel!</b>

00:26.380 --> 00:28.540
<b>You've been summoned by Strategic HQ!</b>

00:33.210 --> 00:38.140
<b><i>If they're calling me at this hour, 
on my "vacation," something must be up.</i></b>

00:38.360 --> 00:42.950
<b><i>Huh... I'm so weirdly 
thirsty for some reason.</i></b>

02:20.160 --> 02:24.990
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

02:20.540 --> 02:22.870
<b><i>With the war in the east bogged down</i></b>

02:23.400 --> 02:25.770
<b><i>and the air war to the west 
getting more intense,</i></b>

02:26.070 --> 02:29.090
<b><i>the Empire needed to reduce
 its attrition in any way possible,</i></b>

02:29.090 --> 02:32.470
<b><i>so it ended its long-running 
battle with the Free Republic,</i></b>

02:32.470 --> 02:35.500
<b><i>deciding to withdraw from 
the southern continent.</i></b>

02:35.500 --> 02:38.510
<b><i>The plan was to return 
its forces via Ildoa,</i></b>

02:38.510 --> 02:41.670
<b><i>in order to emphasize our alliance
 to our enemies.</i></b>

02:42.050 --> 02:43.770
<b><i>That was the plan...</i></b>

02:43.970 --> 02:46.220
<b>Ildoa, Army HQ</b>

02:46.670 --> 02:48.610
<b>You're certain about this?</b>

02:48.610 --> 02:52.240
<b>We're supposed to be their friends...</b>

02:52.690 --> 02:53.850
<b>Yes.</b>

02:53.850 --> 02:58.440
<b>And that's why we volunteered to find a 
path to peace, because they're our allies.</b>

02:58.440 --> 03:00.870
<b>But instead, they say...</b>

03:02.290 --> 03:05.570
<b>"If you're our allies, 
then let us use your roads."</b>

03:06.000 --> 03:10.460
<b>There's still a path 
to peace, I believe...</b>

03:10.460 --> 03:12.330
<b>If they come home with a peace treaty,</b>

03:12.330 --> 03:14.830
<b>I will personally walk them to the door.</b>

03:14.830 --> 03:19.340
<b>But I don't want them 
getting us involved in their war.</b>

03:20.600 --> 03:22.830
<b>You're right there.</b>

03:23.990 --> 03:26.340
<b>"We have refused land passage 
to the Imperial army."</b>

03:24.090 --> 03:26.350
<b>Allied Kingdom Capital, Whitehall</b>

03:26.340 --> 03:29.800
<b>"They'll only be allowed 
at port for 24 hours?"</b>

03:29.800 --> 03:31.840
<b>We couldn't have hoped
 for a better answer.</b>

03:31.840 --> 03:35.970
<b>Yes. Our diplomat has 
certainly done his job.</b>

03:35.970 --> 03:39.320
<b>Ildoa is promising strict neutrality.</b>

03:39.610 --> 03:42.160
<b>They've lost access to 
the shortest land route.</b>

03:42.160 --> 03:46.230
<b>And if the Empire is forced to 
withdraw via a sea route...</b>

03:46.230 --> 03:52.250
<b>They'll be taking an ocean cruise right in
 front of us, the rulers of the seas.</b>

03:52.250 --> 03:54.150
<b>We'll prepare a welcome party.</b>

03:54.150 --> 03:58.700
<b>We can certainly offer them 
more than enough cannon shells...</b>

03:59.330 --> 04:02.950
<b><i>The Allied Kingdom's navy is the strongest
 of any of the major powers.</i></b>

04:02.950 --> 04:08.890
<b><i>The Empire would be badly outgunned 
as it tried to protect its transports.</i></b>

04:09.560 --> 04:12.560
<b>Episode Eight
Torpedo Strike</b>

04:14.670 --> 04:19.770
<b>Men, the majority of the combat team is 
on leave while being reorganized, but...</b>

04:20.080 --> 04:23.200
<b>Yes! As we report directly
 to Strategic HQ,</b>

04:23.200 --> 04:26.820
<b>the 203rd Aerial Battalion
 is an exception!</b>

04:27.630 --> 04:30.340
<b>Now, let me explain the job.</b>

04:30.340 --> 04:33.710
<b>The operation name is Operation Barbaroi.
 As for what we'll be doing...</b>

04:33.710 --> 04:36.500
<b>We're going to be a travel agency.</b>

04:38.160 --> 04:41.870
<b>We'll drive the Allied Kingdom's navy 
from the inner sea,</b>

04:41.870 --> 04:46.710
<b>and bring back General Romel and his men 
from the southern continent.</b>

04:46.910 --> 04:50.220
<b>We'll be welcoming our comrades 
who fought in the south?</b>

04:50.220 --> 04:53.230
<b>We'll need a welcome banquet, then.</b>

04:53.230 --> 04:57.470
<b>May I arrange for some beer 
and wurst for the banquet?</b>

04:58.760 --> 05:03.460
<b>I'm glad you're all in a welcoming mood, 
but General Romel is a popular man.</b>

05:03.460 --> 05:07.070
<b>His heavily armed fans 
will be trying to swarm us.</b>

05:07.310 --> 05:12.040
<b>Then we'll have to give them presents 
full of lead before we say goodbye.</b>

05:12.040 --> 05:14.190
<b>That's the spirit, Lieutenant.</b>

05:14.190 --> 05:17.650
<b>But our naval combat forces in the south 
are almost nonexistent.</b>

05:17.650 --> 05:21.880
<b>We'd have preferred to take 
the safe route via Ildoa.</b>

05:21.880 --> 05:24.300
<b>But they refused to let us through.</b>

05:24.300 --> 05:27.080
<b>Some wonderful allies, huh?</b>

05:27.760 --> 05:29.860
<b>Without the ability to rely on our allies,</b>

05:29.860 --> 05:32.720
<b>we'll have to deal with 
these problems ourselves.</b>

05:32.720 --> 05:37.720
<b>We'll send the Allied Kingdom shits to hell
 right at Ildoa's fucking doorstep!</b>

05:37.720 --> 05:38.800
<b>Yes, ma'am!</b>

05:40.360 --> 05:45.080
<b>We'll be getting a detailed explanation 
of the plan from Strategic HQ.</b>

05:45.080 --> 05:47.030
<b>Salute Colonel Rerugen!</b>

05:48.090 --> 05:48.950
<b>Thank you.</b>

05:49.370 --> 05:52.860
<b>Now, as for Operation Barbaroi...</b>

05:52.860 --> 05:56.570
<b>Lt. Colonel, I'm going to ask you 
to do something difficult.</b>

05:57.900 --> 05:59.500
<b>If necessary, I'll do it.</b>

05:59.810 --> 06:03.380
<b>Thanks... I'm glad to hear that.</b>

06:03.380 --> 06:08.550
<b>Our engineers have prepared something 
that will solve a number of problems.</b>

06:10.370 --> 06:13.700
<b>I'll have him explain.</b>

06:25.970 --> 06:28.730
<b>D-Doktor?!</b>

06:28.730 --> 06:33.280
<b>Oh, it's been so long, 
Lt. Colonel Degurechaff!</b>

06:34.260 --> 06:36.000
<b>I'm so glad you're safe!</b>

06:36.000 --> 06:39.420
<b>God must be protecting you!</b>

06:39.420 --> 06:40.880
<b>S-Sure...</b>

06:40.880 --> 06:44.880
<b>Oh, you're worried about whether 
you'll be able to protect your comrades!</b>

06:44.880 --> 06:46.190
<b>Don't worry!</b>

06:46.190 --> 06:48.540
<b>Leave it all to me!</b>

06:48.540 --> 06:51.970
<b>I have prepared something 
that's key to this operation!</b>

06:52.300 --> 06:55.300
<b>Behold! This is it!</b>

06:55.700 --> 06:57.530
<b>The V-2!</b>

06:57.530 --> 07:01.480
<b>A revolutionary weapon, 
brought to us by the grace of God!</b>

07:01.480 --> 07:05.430
<b>A guided torpedo, 
wreathed in the mantle of faith!</b>

07:07.080 --> 07:10.240
<b><i>Is that... a pilot's seat?</i></b>

07:10.650 --> 07:14.250
<b>Looking back, the V-1 only flew straight.</b>

07:14.250 --> 07:19.850
<b>Like my faith, it could only 
go forward! Only forward!</b>

07:19.850 --> 07:23.440
<b>Straight on to the promised land!</b>

07:23.960 --> 07:29.690
<b>But the V-2 can head to its destination 
freely with a believer in tow!</b>

07:29.690 --> 07:34.090
<b>Call it a weapon that enables one 
to confront the harshness of reality!</b>

07:35.060 --> 07:38.470
<b><i>Wh-What the hell is
 the Doktor talking about?!</i></b>

07:39.960 --> 07:44.720
<b>Whatever path it takes, it will arrive 
at the shining paradise on the hill...</b>

07:44.990 --> 07:48.150
<b>To recreate the journey to the holy land,</b>

07:48.150 --> 07:51.860
<b>I have given the V-2 incredible 
guidance capabilities!</b>

07:51.860 --> 07:55.080
<b>So that it shall never become lost,</b>

07:55.080 --> 07:58.240
<b>just like you who are 
guided by your faith!</b>

07:59.660 --> 08:02.320
<b><i>I'm an atheist, you know...</i></b>

08:02.320 --> 08:04.300
<b>But fret not, Lt. Colonel!</b>

08:04.300 --> 08:07.250
<b>I won't be stealing 
your thunder, of course!</b>

08:07.250 --> 08:11.630
<b>We are friends, 
both praising the glory of God!</b>

08:13.170 --> 08:15.990
<b>It's used the same as the V-1.</b>

08:15.990 --> 08:19.090
<b>You can just slam it into the enemy!</b>

08:19.330 --> 08:22.350
<b>Oh, but don't forget to 
bail out at the last second.</b>

08:22.350 --> 08:28.730
<b>You'll get to watch up close as its huge 
explosive load blows away your troubles!</b>

08:29.360 --> 08:32.690
<b>What guarantee is there that 
we won't be caught in the blast?</b>

08:32.690 --> 08:36.920
<b>Well, that's up to the Lord.</b>

08:36.920 --> 08:40.110
<b>Which means you don't have to 
worry about a thing, I assume!</b>

08:41.550 --> 08:44.920
<b>Lt. Colonel, I understand your concerns.</b>

08:44.920 --> 08:48.600
<b>Especially with a new torpedo, 
given the troubles the current ones have.</b>

08:48.600 --> 08:50.290
<b>No need to fear!</b>

08:50.290 --> 08:54.740
<b>This is totally different from the eels 
those incompetents in the navy dreamed up!</b>

08:54.740 --> 08:59.350
<b>I have taken the greatest care, 
down to each individual fuse!</b>

08:59.350 --> 09:01.130
<b>These are my torpedoes—</b>

09:03.220 --> 09:07.150
<b>I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!</b>

09:09.010 --> 09:14.090
<b>Would you please forgive my pride, 
Lt. Colonel Degurechaff?</b>

09:14.090 --> 09:15.580
<b>D-Doktor?</b>

09:15.580 --> 09:20.140
<b>I almost gave myself over to arrogance!</b>

09:20.140 --> 09:25.330
<b>Even though it was our working together 
that made this miracle possible!</b>

09:26.170 --> 09:31.300
<b>The V-2 was created thanks 
to your proposal and advice!</b>

09:31.300 --> 09:35.460
<b>It was a product of faith, 
made by two believers!</b>

09:35.460 --> 09:37.310
<b>Truly...</b>

09:37.310 --> 09:40.540
<b>It is our child! Yours and mine!</b>

09:43.180 --> 09:50.690
<b>Several
Months
Earlier</b>

09:44.120 --> 09:50.190
<b><i>Once, I was invited by the engineers
to give my opinion as a field officer.</i></b>

09:50.690 --> 09:59.950
<b>Imperial Army Logistics Command,
Engineering Research Unit</b>

09:50.960 --> 09:55.170
<b>In the end, without enough 
guns for our main warships,</b>

09:55.170 --> 09:56.660
<b>we won't achieve command of the seas,</b>

09:56.660 --> 09:59.520
<b>or even threaten 
the enemy's control over them.</b>

09:59.940 --> 10:02.750
<b>In the long term, you're correct.</b>

10:02.750 --> 10:07.250
<b>But fighting without a plan for the now 
would only be a waste of money.</b>

10:07.700 --> 10:10.630
<b>You're correct in theory. But so what?</b>

10:10.630 --> 10:13.750
<b>Do you have a short-term solution?</b>

10:13.970 --> 10:16.530
<b>I do. Torpedoes,</b>

10:16.530 --> 10:19.770
<b>especially those dropped by air, 
would be extremely effective, I believe.</b>

10:19.770 --> 10:23.850
<b>Our technology isn't even sufficient 
for proper ship-based torpedoes.</b>

10:23.850 --> 10:26.150
<b>Air-dropped torpedoes would 
be even more difficult...</b>

10:26.440 --> 10:29.480
<b>Why not change how we use them?</b>

10:29.480 --> 10:31.510
<b>Using submarines to whittle 
down their numbers...</b>

10:31.510 --> 10:35.150
<b>Could a slow-moving sub hit a warship?</b>

10:35.150 --> 10:37.760
<b>There's no way a novice could come up</b>

10:37.760 --> 10:40.520
<b>with some idea that would 
instantly turn things around.</b>

10:40.940 --> 10:45.910
<b>Why not put a mage in the torpedo, then?</b>

10:46.370 --> 10:47.280
<b>What?</b>

10:47.280 --> 10:52.170
<b>The mage could guide it to the enemy 
and bail out at the last second.</b>

10:52.170 --> 10:54.600
<b>It would never miss.</b>

10:54.600 --> 10:57.620
<b>And a mage could continue the attack 
after the torpedo strike.</b>

11:04.290 --> 11:08.130
<b><i>I think I did say that, actually...</i></b>

11:08.130 --> 11:11.180
<b><i>I guess anybody can throw out "good ideas"</i></b>

11:11.180 --> 11:15.020
<b><i>as long as they think they're not 
gonna be the one to actually do them.</i></b>

11:15.380 --> 11:18.320
<b><i>Is this another trick of Being X's?</i></b>

11:18.320 --> 11:19.950
<b><i>I bet it is.</i></b>

11:19.950 --> 11:21.530
<b><i>It's the only explanation!</i></b>

11:21.530 --> 11:24.530
<b><i>Well, fine. Fine.</i></b>

11:24.530 --> 11:27.160
<b><i>If that's your game...</i></b>

11:29.930 --> 11:31.510
<b><i>I'm just going to beat it!</i></b>

11:38.000 --> 11:41.510
<b>July 15th, Unified Year 1927</b>

11:41.510 --> 11:44.510
<b>Southern Continent Churos Military Port</b>

11:49.380 --> 11:52.880
<b>General, everyone's ready to board.</b>

11:52.880 --> 11:55.230
<b>But will we be able to 
withdraw successfully?</b>

11:55.480 --> 12:01.990
<b>Commander in Charge of
the Southern Continent Expedition
General Romel</b>

11:55.510 --> 11:59.410
<b>It seems there are more Allied Kingdom 
ships waiting for us than expected.</b>

11:59.410 --> 12:02.880
<b>Will we really make it across the sea?</b>

12:05.740 --> 12:16.630
<b>Same Day, Off the Coast of Dakal</b>

12:19.340 --> 12:20.660
<b>Signals on sonar.</b>

12:20.660 --> 12:22.180
<b>Warship engines!</b>

12:22.180 --> 12:23.890
<b>Multiple main warship class signals!</b>

12:24.470 --> 12:27.500
<b>Lt. Colonel Degurechaff, we have contact.</b>

12:27.500 --> 12:29.230
<b>Multiple large ships.</b>

12:29.230 --> 12:31.630
<b>How wonderful.</b>

12:31.900 --> 12:34.310
<b>A heavy cruiser for an appetizer.</b>

12:34.310 --> 12:36.890
<b>And a carrier and a battleship 
for the main courses.</b>

12:36.890 --> 12:39.840
<b>But it's just before sunset, 
unfortunately.</b>

12:39.840 --> 12:42.280
<b>We can use the eels instead of V-2s...</b>

12:42.280 --> 12:44.600
<b>I appreciate your kindness.</b>

12:44.600 --> 12:47.830
<b>But if we want to be certain this works, 
we should be the ones to do it.</b>

12:48.620 --> 12:50.990
<b>Normally, I'd agree.</b>

12:50.990 --> 12:54.760
<b>But at this hour, 
where visibility is so poor...</b>

12:55.190 --> 12:57.480
<b>That's why we're here.</b>

12:57.480 --> 12:59.810
<b>We're just going to have to do this.</b>

13:00.430 --> 13:03.680
<b>Because our allies' retreat depends on us?</b>

13:04.760 --> 13:08.800
<b>And our friends in Ildoa 
are watching, too.</b>

13:08.800 --> 13:12.390
<b>We, the ones on the front lines, 
will have to make this all work out.</b>

13:12.390 --> 13:15.110
<b>We'll bring the goddess 
of luck to our side,</b>

13:15.110 --> 13:18.090
<b>if we have to kick her ass 
and drag her over to do it.</b>

13:25.740 --> 13:27.860
<b>Final confirmation before we board.</b>

13:27.860 --> 13:29.110
<b>Yes, ma'am!</b>

13:29.360 --> 13:31.920
<b>We have only 12 V-2s.</b>

13:31.920 --> 13:34.090
<b>We'll have to make good use of them.</b>

13:34.090 --> 13:36.780
<b>We need to take out the carrier 
and the battleship no matter what.</b>

13:36.780 --> 13:38.570
<b>Don't get the target order wrong.</b>

13:38.570 --> 13:41.960
<b>Just before the torpedoes hit, 
bail out and surface.</b>

13:41.960 --> 13:44.330
<b>Then engage the destroyers in combat.</b>

13:46.720 --> 13:48.260
<b>What's with those looks?</b>

13:48.480 --> 13:52.340
<b>Lt. Colonel, this is... it's too...</b>

13:52.340 --> 13:54.320
<b>Too what?</b>

13:54.320 --> 13:56.550
<b>As commanding officer, 
I'm going in first.</b>

13:56.550 --> 13:58.500
<b>All you have to do is follow me.</b>

13:58.500 --> 14:00.720
<b>Nothing more and nothing less.</b>

14:01.020 --> 14:04.940
<b>H-How are we supposed to 
identify the enemy underwater?</b>

14:11.490 --> 14:13.290
<b>Um, about oxygen...</b>

14:14.580 --> 14:17.580
<b>Special Edition!
The Secrets of
the Mage Units'
Strength!</b>

14:17.870 --> 14:22.080
<b>Mages can
generate
their own
oxygen for
 high-altitude
combat!</b>

14:22.690 --> 14:25.260
<b>I'm concerned about water 
pressure and the currents...</b>

14:27.760 --> 14:32.820
<b>And that's why we mages are 
absolutely needed for this plan.</b>

14:33.300 --> 14:35.350
<b>We'll just have to pray it works out.</b>

14:35.350 --> 14:37.100
<b>Pray?</b>

14:37.440 --> 14:39.160
<b>I'm sorry, Lieutenant...</b>

14:39.160 --> 14:41.100
<b>But first, do every damn thing you can.</b>

14:42.020 --> 14:44.650
<b>Human strength! Human will!</b>

14:44.650 --> 14:45.720
<b>That's what it takes...</b>

14:49.870 --> 14:52.190
<b>to do what must be done.</b>

14:52.830 --> 14:56.100
<b>We've got the target's courses and speed!</b>

14:56.100 --> 14:58.050
<b>Lt. Colonel, we're sending the data.</b>

14:58.050 --> 14:59.670
<b>But be aware they're approximate.</b>

14:59.930 --> 15:02.670
<b>Very well. Data received.</b>

15:02.670 --> 15:05.350
<b>Final check. Prepare for launch!</b>

15:07.760 --> 15:11.340
<b>Very good. Looks like 
everyone's ready, right?</b>

15:11.640 --> 15:12.470
<b>Yes.</b>

15:12.470 --> 15:14.220
<b>Uh... yes.</b>

15:14.530 --> 15:15.560
<b>Uh...</b>

15:15.560 --> 15:16.860
<b>Good.</b>

15:16.860 --> 15:19.520
<b>I'm glad... very glad... to hear it!</b>

15:21.290 --> 15:22.300
<b>Here we go!</b>

15:46.340 --> 15:50.590
<b>Allied Kingdom Second Fleet</b>

15:50.980 --> 15:53.800
<b>So we wipe out the enemy 
as they try to flee into the night</b>

15:53.800 --> 15:56.680
<b>and finish up operations on 
the southern continent, huh?</b>

15:56.680 --> 15:58.630
<b>Easy job, huh?</b>

15:58.630 --> 16:01.100
<b>They don't stand a chance.</b>

16:08.880 --> 16:10.320
<b><i>I-Is it time yet?</i></b>

16:11.180 --> 16:12.200
<b><i>Not yet...</i></b>

16:12.630 --> 16:13.760
<b><i>Not yet...</i></b>

16:14.710 --> 16:16.110
<b><i>I can't go on!</i></b>

16:16.110 --> 16:17.130
<b><i>Now!</i></b>

16:36.460 --> 16:37.760
<b>W-What's going on?</b>

16:37.760 --> 16:40.000
<b>The Mighty Hood!</b>

16:40.000 --> 16:42.130
<b>The Ark Royal!</b>

16:48.530 --> 16:50.260
<b>We're doomed!</b>

16:53.670 --> 16:54.790
<b>Reinforcements!</b>

16:54.790 --> 16:56.380
<b>Reinforcements from the main fleet!</b>

16:56.380 --> 16:58.990
<b>A blessing! Oh, thank you, God!</b>

16:58.990 --> 17:00.550
<b>We're saved!</b>

17:00.550 --> 17:02.490
<b>God didn't abandon us?!</b>

17:07.260 --> 17:08.800
<b>Get over here!</b>

17:08.800 --> 17:10.500
<b>Over here!</b>

17:13.630 --> 17:15.460
<b>Enemy mages off the starboard bow!</b>

17:15.460 --> 17:16.220
<b>What?</b>

17:24.220 --> 17:27.150
<b>Why? Has the Lord abandoned us?!</b>

17:27.150 --> 17:30.140
<b>Go to hell, you piece of shit god!</b>

17:30.140 --> 17:33.130
<b>Before you pray, get to work.</b>

17:33.130 --> 17:35.170
<b>If talking is the first thing you do,</b>

17:35.170 --> 17:36.910
<b>you're worthless!</b>

17:46.160 --> 17:48.240
<b><i>Did you see that, Being X?</i></b>

17:48.240 --> 17:51.460
<b><i>I'm not losing to one of 
your ridiculous trials!</i></b>

17:51.800 --> 17:55.600
<b><i>Behold my stubbornness and pride 
as someone living in modern times!</i></b>

18:01.500 --> 18:04.530
<b><i>The will of God can go fuck itself.</i></b>

18:04.530 --> 18:09.070
<b><i>I will survive and live off royalties, 
no matter what I have to do.</i></b>

18:10.750 --> 18:14.310
<b>I'm Major Otto von Elm, captain of U-091.</b>

18:14.310 --> 18:16.630
<b>Wonderful work, Lt. Colonel.</b>

18:17.560 --> 18:21.010
<b>The Allied Kingdom's 
main fleet has withdrawn,</b>

18:21.010 --> 18:23.970
<b>and the southern expeditionary force 
is in for a lovely sea voyage.</b>

18:23.970 --> 18:27.570
<b>My old school chum, Barchet, 
was so excited.</b>

18:27.570 --> 18:31.320
<b>Oh, you went to officers' school 
with Captain Barchet.</b>

18:31.320 --> 18:32.710
<b>I had no idea.</b>

18:32.710 --> 18:36.890
<b>Oh, this is for you. It's from HQ.</b>

18:41.620 --> 18:43.810
<b>Oh, I see.</b>

18:43.800 --> 18:50.310
<b>Ildoa
Kingdom
Entry
Pass</b>

18:44.420 --> 18:50.310
<b><i>We're going to take advantage of their 
24-hour limit and limits on personnel?</i></b>

18:50.730 --> 18:55.600
<b><i>I think I'm going to enjoy 
a little sightseeing trip then.</i></b>

19:12.460 --> 19:18.100
<b>"Is it not a joy to have 
friends come from afar?"</b>

19:18.100 --> 19:20.820
<b>May I answer that, "If people 
do not recognize your worth,</b>

19:20.820 --> 19:24.090
<b>but this does not worry you, 
are you not a true gentleman?"</b>

19:24.090 --> 19:26.420
<b>Whatever do you mean?</b>

19:26.420 --> 19:29.690
<b>As your allies, we understand you well.</b>

19:29.960 --> 19:32.710
<b>A laurel wreath for the victors, then?</b>

19:33.370 --> 19:36.820
<b>The Allied Kingdom's fleet 
lost the battle a little too hard.</b>

19:36.820 --> 19:41.320
<b>So of course we're willing to make 
minor adjustments to our policies.</b>

19:41.320 --> 19:45.660
<b>We're a neutral country. 
We're allowed to do that after all.</b>

19:46.200 --> 19:49.530
<b><i>The Ildoans are completely shameless.</i></b>

19:49.820 --> 19:53.460
<b><i>No wonder the folks back home 
want to teach them a lesson.</i></b>

19:53.460 --> 19:55.620
<b><i>They're not welcoming a military unit.</i></b>

19:55.620 --> 19:58.370
<b><i>Just twelve people on a courtesy visit.</i></b>

19:58.370 --> 20:03.130
<b><i>But even if the Ildoans say that, 
it's still a mage unit.</i></b>

20:03.130 --> 20:05.440
<b><i>A nice bit of humiliation.</i></b>

20:06.180 --> 20:07.750
<b><i>My head hurts.</i></b>

20:07.750 --> 20:12.070
<b><i>Why did it have to be Lt. Colonel 
Degurechaff's unit that we're allowing in?</i></b>

20:12.070 --> 20:15.220
<b><i>From a diplomatic 
perspective, this hurts!</i></b>

20:15.850 --> 20:18.550
<b>I can't wait to see 
Lt. Colonel Degurechaff!</b>

20:18.550 --> 20:21.720
<b>She was quite helpful to me in the east.</b>

20:21.720 --> 20:25.200
<b>I'm so happy she's paying us 
this courtesy visit!</b>

20:25.200 --> 20:28.600
<b><i>I'm so glad I managed to meet 
that monster ahead of time!</i></b>

20:28.600 --> 20:32.790
<b><i>I don't think I could've kept it together 
if this were the first time I met her.</i></b>

20:32.790 --> 20:35.630
<b>So it will be a heartwarming 
reunion, then?</b>

20:35.630 --> 20:39.490
<b>I'd like to do something special 
to commemorate it.</b>

20:39.490 --> 20:41.570
<b>Of course! But unfortunately,</b>

20:41.570 --> 20:45.790
<b>it's so sudden we lack the facilities
and budget for a proper welcome.</b>

20:45.790 --> 20:49.620
<b><i>Sheesh. This whole thing is a farce, 
through and through.</i></b>

20:49.620 --> 20:53.560
<b><i>They're having their "friends" 
come in through the back door,</i></b>

20:53.560 --> 20:55.320
<b><i>with nobody around to see them.</i></b>

20:55.710 --> 20:59.520
<b><i>But all we're doing is quietly 
allowing in a single submarine.</i></b>

20:59.520 --> 21:01.190
<b><i>As long as they don't make a fuss...</i></b>

21:17.450 --> 21:19.310
<b>Hello! Hello!</b>

21:19.310 --> 21:22.970
<b>Thank you so much for the welcome, 
my Ildoan friends!</b>

21:26.870 --> 21:32.920
<b><i>I-Is it really okay... is it really 
okay for her to stand out this much?</i></b>

23:13.030 --> 23:16.660
<b>Good luck! Work hard!</b>

23:17.060 --> 23:21.730
<b>Um... you're a mage. 
You're not going, Captain?</b>

23:22.180 --> 23:23.250
<b>I can't fit.</b>

23:24.980 --> 23:27.350
<b>I can't fit into the swimsuit.</b>

23:30.510 --> 23:35.170
<b>Good luck! Work hard!</b>

23:35.970 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time
Sightseeing Tour</b>
